1/ Code contracts enable developers to write software that is more robust to the mistakes made by other developers. They provide static verification of the code, helping to write more reliable code. 

2/ Pex, Microsoft's automated unit test generator, can generate automatic unit tests that cover the entire codebase, ensuring that it is thoroughly tested.

3/ The PexGenerated.cs file contains the automatically generated tests that Pex creates, with additional code contracts added for custom assertions and observations.

