**Coding Test Automation with Programming – Pex**

Pex is a static analysis tool for software testing developed by Microsoft Research. The tool's aim is to help developers understand their code base better by automatically exploring the code branching paths and generating test cases. It is a part of Microsoft's Test Professional Tools suite.
https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=16470

Microsoft Research's Pex is a code coverage tool for testing, that is an extension to Microsoft's Visual Studio 2017. It is designed to automatically generate a large number of test cases to verify that the software is behaving as expected.

Pex scans the program and identifies the paths that the program can take during its execution. For each of these paths, it creates a test which will explore every possible combination of values in the program.

For more information: http://research.microsoft.com/en-us/um/cambridge/projects/automated-testing/

(https://github.com/Microsoft/VisualStudio-UnitTesting-Samples/tree/master/PexSamples)

